50,000 vectors of 512 numbers

brute force          10.7 ms per query   recall 100% by definition

M=8   ef_construction=40   built in   10.3s
     ef_search=10   recall@10  84.4%     0.05 ms     218x faster than exact
     ef_search=25   recall@10  86.6%     0.06 ms     173x faster than exact
     ef_search=50   recall@10  86.6%     0.12 ms      85x faster than exact
     ef_search=100  recall@10  86.8%     0.14 ms      77x faster than exact
     ef_search=200  recall@10  86.8%     0.23 ms      47x faster than exact

M=32  ef_construction=200  built in  195.6s
     ef_search=10   recall@10  96.4%     0.10 ms     110x faster than exact
     ef_search=25   recall@10  96.2%     0.11 ms      94x faster than exact
     ef_search=50   recall@10  96.2%     0.18 ms      58x faster than exact
     ef_search=100  recall@10  96.4%     0.28 ms      38x faster than exact
     ef_search=200  recall@10  96.4%     0.44 ms      24x faster than exact

Across a twentyfold range, ef_search moved recall 2.4 points at M=8 and
0.2 at M=32; changing M moved it 10.1 points on average.
Which dial binds depends on the data — and 48,546 of these vectors are random noise,
the hardest data an index can be given. The next listing checks that.
